Diabetic Autonomic Neuropathy with GI Manifestations vs Chronic Constipation with Impaction:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal bloating, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, bloating, feeling of incomplete evacuation, hard stools, headache\n\nDiabetic Autonomic Neuropathy with GI Manifestations vs Infectious Gastroenteritis:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal bloating, abdominal obesity, abnormal cardiac septum morphology, abnormal cardiac ventricular function\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea\n\nChronic Constipation with Impaction vs Infectious Gastroenteritis:\n  Favours first:  bloating, feeling of incomplete evacuation, hard stools, headache, infrequent bowel movements\n  Favours second: abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches\n\nRelated to Diabetic Autonomic Neuropathy with GI Manifestations: autonomic neuropathy, diabetic neuropathy\n\nRelated to Infectious Gastroenteritis: campylobacteriosis, colitis (disease), enteritis\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → feeding difficulties → Diabetic Autonomic Neuropathy with GI Manifestations\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → abdominal pain → Infectious Gastroenteritis\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → vomiting → Infectious Gastroenteritis"}
